From 91b05be5da5f62567701489519804b7bba91c54f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anuj Gupta <anuj1072538@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 12:24:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] block: fix dma-buf iter handling in blk_rq_map_user_iov()

blk_rq_map_user_iov() selects map_bvec=true only for ITER_BVEC, causing
dma-buf iterators to fall into the !user_backed_iter() -> copy=true
bounce-copy path.  dma-buf iters are already page-backed by device DMA
mappings; treat them like bvec and map directly.

Without this, NVMe passthrough I/O with a registered dma-buf silently
uses a bounce buffer, discarding the read data back to user space.

Signed-off-by: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
---
 block/blk-map.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/block/blk-map.c b/block/blk-map.c
index 9cb9605d1f62..8016b49f09f7 100644
--- a/block/blk-map.c
+++ b/block/blk-map.c
@@ -510,7 +510,7 @@ int blk_rq_map_user_iov(struct request_queue *q, struct request *rq,
 		copy = true;
 	else if (iov_iter_alignment(iter) & align)
 		copy = true;
-	else if (iov_iter_is_bvec(iter))
+	else if (iov_iter_is_bvec(iter) || iov_iter_is_dmabuf_map(iter))
 		map_bvec = true;
 	else if (!user_backed_iter(iter))
 		copy = true;
